==English==
{{was wotd|2024|May|25}}

===Etymology===
{{root|en|ine-pro|*wer-|id=heed}}
The {{glossary|noun}} is a variant of {{m|en|Milaner|t=(''obsolete'') inhabitant or native of Milan}} (referring to the importation and sale of women’s apparel, etc., made in Milan: see {{senseno|en|seller}}), from Late {{inh|en|enm|Milener}}, {{m|enm|Miloner|t=native of Milan}},<ref>{{R:MED Online|entry=Milener|pos=n|id=MED27761}}</ref> from {{m|enm|Milan}}<ref>{{R:MED Online|entry=Milan|pos=n|id=MED27736}}</ref> + {{m|enm|-er|-er(e)|pos={{glossary|suffix}} denoting an inhabitant or resident}}.<ref>{{R:MED Online|entry=-ē̆r(e|pos=''suf.''(1)|noformat=1|id=MED14294}}</ref><ref>Compare {{R:OED Online|pos=n|id=8703772192|date=March 2024|nodot=1}}; {{R:Lexico|pos=n|us=1}}</ref>

The {{glossary|verb}} is derived from the noun.<ref>{{R:OED Online|pos=v|id=2130102995|date=July 2023}}</ref>

